  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1018 PM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nThis weekend will begin a more unsettled weather pattern as a\ntrough digs southward across the Great Lakes region on Saturday \nand Sunday. Ensembles differ in the handling of this trough with \nthe EPS showing a stronger trough closing off to our north and the\nGEFS remaining an open wave over the Ohio River Valley into early\nnext week. Regardless, rain and storm chances will increase this \nweekend into early next week as moisture filters back into the \narea. Temps should remain at or below normal during the day with \nmilder overnight lows. We will have to wait and see for the finer\ndetails of any severe threat that may evolve as models become \nmore in sync in the coming days. Make sure to check back if\nplanning anything outside this weekend as the forecast can and\nwill likely change.",
